# Architecture

Source: `governance/architecture/architecture-governance.md`

- Architecture decisions are human decisions. AI analyses, proposes alternatives, documents.
- Follow the existing architecture and accepted ADRs. Consistency beats theoretical improvement.
- Never introduce a pattern, layer or framework only because it is "best practice".
- ADR required for: new layer/module boundary, new pattern, framework change, breaking API change,
  shared data model change or migration, new external integration, cross-cutting concerns.
- Every ADR: Context, Decision, Alternatives (incl. "keep current"), Consequences (incl. negative), Status, Date.
  Template: `templates/adr.md`. Only a human sets status `Accepted`.
- Contract first: agree interfaces before parallel frontend/backend work (`orchestration/workflows/fullstack.md`).
- Major architecture changes are HIGH risk → plan approval required.

